            "review_title": "Review at Sushi Boy",
            "review_text": "Anh N\nAdelaide, Australia7 contributions\n0\nAmazing Hidden Spot - Eat likes locals\nAug 2016 • Friends\nLocation: right on one of the most well known street for tourists and backpackers in Hochiminh city. But I call it a hidden spot because you have to find your way from the back of 135 Bui Vien and challenge yourself walking up stair to level 4. Despite the the building and the stair are quite messy and rustic, Sushi Boy is delightedly stand out from its surrounding, clean and quiet space. You will have a good view from the balcony to observe local lifestyle from high above if you sit outside (night time is better)\n\nFood: Fresh, tasty and affordable... I highly recommend you to try the Sashimi, Dragon Roll, Volcano Ship and Sea Urchin Roe. Best price in town to compare to other restaurant as the same level of fresh and quality food. There are various ranges of Japanese food (included Udon, Rice and Soba) and Alcohol. I personally like the coke float, plum wine or their homemade peach ice tea for drink. I appreciate the way the owner really concerns about food hygiene (it's a highlighted problem in Vietnam)\n\nServices: Very helpful and friendly. They go beyond themselves to explain everything about the menu and recommend you some good stuff to try. Very often come back to check if you are happy with your meal or need anything else. If you love Japanese food and have a chance to talk to the owner, a young and passionate guy, your conversation seems like never ends.\n\nI came there with a group of friends and everyone had a pleasure experience. Will definitely come back next time I'm in Hochiminh city\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten September 2, 2016",
